{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Every time I try to drag a patient's visit to a different doctor or time slot, the system throws an error code and wipes out the attached clinical notes. This is happening multiple times a day and slowing down our front desk completely. Please fix this bug immediately.",
   "id": "gen-071",
   "subject": "Error when rescheduling patient visits"
  },
  {
   "body": "We noticed that our monthly billing subscription was charged twice for this invoice period. I checked our account statements and there is a duplicate charge. Please reverse this incorrect fee and credit our account back right away.",
   "id": "gen-072",
   "subject": "Duplicate subscription charge on invoice"
  },
  {
   "body": "I'm completely unable to sign off on incoming lab panels today because the signature button is grayed out. I need these filed before leaving for clinic hours, so please look into this right away.",
   "id": "gen-073",
   "subject": "Cannot sign off on lab reports"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am trying to figure out how the portal handles the waiting period for sensitive test results, but the settings menu is completely baffling. Where do I go to change the automatic release delay so patients don't see results instantly?",
   "id": "gen-074",
   "subject": "Confused about test result release settings"
  },
  {
   "body": "Good morning. I am writing to see if there is a way to streamline how our clinic handles incoming diagnostic files. Right now, reviewing every single routine panel and annotating notes takes a lot of clicks, especially when I want to batch-sign normal results while keeping abnormal ones flagged for a deeper look. I looked through the settings under my user profile and reviewed the documentation online, but I couldn't find a clear workflow for setting up custom filters or quick-sign macros. Could you let me know if our current subscription tier supports advanced lab queue sorting, or if there is a specific configuration my admin needs to turn on for my account?",
   "id": "gen-075",
   "subject": "Question regarding lab review workflow customization"
  },
  {
   "body": "I'm trying to figure out where we set up automatic alerts for urgent lab values, but nothing in the admin menu makes sense. Can someone point me to the right settings screen?",
   "id": "gen-076",
   "subject": "Where are critical lab alert settings?"
  },
  {
   "body": "Patients are complaining that their credit card copay payments are failing on the portal checkout page. Fix this error now.",
   "id": "gen-077",
   "subject": "Portal credit card payments failing"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello support team, I am terribly sorry to bother you with this, but our diagnostic feed seems to have stopped working sometime late yesterday afternoon. We noticed this morning that incoming electronic results from our primary reference lab are not populating into patient charts automatically. I tried restarting our local interface gateway and checking the connection status page in our settings, but the status indicator just keeps spinning without loading anything. Could you please look on your end to see if our data feed connection dropped or if there is an update we missed? Thank you so much for your help.",
   "id": "gen-078",
   "subject": "Incoming lab interface feed not populating charts"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, we recently brought on a new medical assistant who needs access to the system. Could you please provide instructions on how to set up their user account and assign the appropriate staff role? Once they are in, I also need to deactivate an old account for someone who left last month.",
   "id": "gen-079",
   "subject": "Adding new staff member and deactivating old user"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am so tired of dealing with out-of-stock medication alerts that lead to nowhere. Every time a pharmacy rejects a drug, the software doesn't give me a clear way to swap it out without starting a brand new prescription from scratch. Can we please get this workflow fixed?",
   "id": "gen-080",
   "subject": "Medication substitution workflow is terrible"
  }
 ]
}
